{
 "schema_version": 1,
 "purpose": "simulation Phase 4d (#841): sm.settrop then sm.corrupt, run by CASA and by casa-rs",
 "notes": [
  "Each scenario predicts a 1 Jy point at the phase centre, so its noise-free twin's parallel hands are 1: DATA over the twin is each row's g_p(c) conj(g_q(c)), which compare_sm_ms.py checks against the scenario's Tf Jones table, channel by channel, on each side.",
  "CASA's phase in channel c is the fractional water-vapour excess delta times ATM's dispersive wet phase delay on its grid half a band below the channel; casa-rs's is delta times the whole wet phase delay at CHAN_FREQ (docs/CASA (C++) bugs.md). compare_sm_ms.py recovers delta from each side's table through its own model, with its own ATM's delays (CASA's through casatools' at tool, casa-rs's through casa-atmosphere, --atmosphere-model), and checks that it is one value per solution across the channels; casa-rs's is held to the documented deltapwv, CASA's reported (its series normalise with values read past their transforms).",
  "1 mm of water vapour fluctuating by 1 % keeps casa-rs's phases well inside half a turn across the 183 GHz line, so the excess is read without unwrapping.",
  "No autocorrelations: CASA's autocorrelation rows reset their antenna's T to 1, which casa-rs does not follow.",
  "Two windows of 64 channels: across the 183.31 GHz line (from 180 GHz, 100 MHz) and at 230 GHz (15.625 MHz); casa-rs does not yet write windows of different shapes in one MeasurementSet.",
  "Seven 12 m antennas in sm_atm_scenarios.json's layout: CASA 6.7.6's sm.predict of a component list segfaults on that layout's mix of 12 m and 7 m dishes, before any settrop."
 ],
